WEBVTT

00:53.720 --> 00:54.930
Kusimayu!

00:55.931 --> 00:58.517
Sweetie, lunch is ready.

00:59.518 --> 01:02.187
We made your favorite.

01:10.487 --> 01:12.114
Is that it?

01:12.656 --> 01:14.825
That's it.

01:15.284 --> 01:17.077
Not much longer now.

01:17.578 --> 01:22.499
Are you excited… or nervous?

01:25.043 --> 01:26.712
Excited.

01:27.462 --> 01:29.965
Except I've been sweeping this one spot

01:30.048 --> 01:31.967
for half an hour.

01:32.467 --> 01:34.928
We noticed.

01:35.012 --> 01:37.931
It's very clean.

03:47.936 --> 03:51.899
The sky is such a deep blue today.

03:52.733 --> 03:55.152
And the air smells good.

03:55.611 --> 03:58.071
It feels hopeful.

04:23.013 --> 04:25.015
Is it here?

04:25.098 --> 04:26.099
Yes.

04:28.060 --> 04:29.937
Don't be scared, love.

04:31.230 --> 04:33.482
I'm not.

05:53.478 --> 05:54.813
Will it hurt?

05:54.897 --> 05:58.066
No, Kusimayu. Not one bit.

05:58.150 --> 06:02.821
We would never hurt you.

06:05.449 --> 06:06.783
Are you ready?

06:19.463 --> 06:24.134
Three… two… one…

09:26.525 --> 09:28.652
How long till he gets here?

09:28.735 --> 09:29.945
About two hours.

09:34.199 --> 09:37.286
This is the guy I yelled at
when we were on the plane?

09:38.287 --> 09:39.830
You had a lot on your mind.

09:44.960 --> 09:46.170
And he's in an ambulance?

09:50.507 --> 09:51.508
Long story.

09:55.429 --> 09:56.430
What does he want?

09:57.681 --> 09:59.683
He won't talk to us. So…

10:02.686 --> 10:04.271
He did receive your first video.

10:04.771 --> 10:05.772
Yeah?

10:06.732 --> 10:09.359
Maybe he's heeding your call?

10:14.364 --> 10:15.949
We're thinking…

10:16.033 --> 10:17.492
I'm thinking…

10:18.827 --> 10:22.289
I probably shouldn't be here
when he arrives.

10:23.040 --> 10:24.291
It would upset him.

10:25.542 --> 10:29.963
You don't have to be here either, Carol.
It's completely up to you.

10:35.010 --> 10:38.764
All the way from… Paraguay?

10:40.265 --> 10:42.684
Well, hell. I owe it to him, don't I?

10:44.228 --> 10:46.313
I'll just hear him out
and send him on his way.

10:47.814 --> 10:50.192
I mean, it's not like
he's dangerous, is he?

10:56.281 --> 10:57.991
Is he? Dangerous?

11:02.287 --> 11:04.081
We don't think he'd ever hurt you.

11:57.134 --> 11:58.927
My name is Manousos Oviedo.

12:59.655 --> 13:01.281
My name is Manousos Oviedo.

13:02.699 --> 13:04.368
I am not one of them.

13:05.452 --> 13:06.787
I wish to save the world.

13:10.290 --> 13:13.293
Hola. Me llamo Carol Sturka.

13:14.586 --> 13:17.589
Bienvenidos to… to… mi casa.

13:21.552 --> 13:22.553
Hi.

13:23.887 --> 13:24.888
Hablamos?

13:27.349 --> 13:29.768
Yes. Yes, we talk.

13:30.602 --> 13:34.773
Pe… Pero… No, no machete.

13:36.191 --> 13:38.026
I no dangerous.

13:46.034 --> 13:47.035
It's safe.

14:04.052 --> 14:05.804
Okay. Aquí?

14:14.730 --> 14:16.315
We talk in here.

14:18.108 --> 14:20.194
Let's hablamos en mi casa.

14:22.404 --> 14:24.364
Maybe better? Mejor?

14:26.533 --> 14:27.784
We talk in the ambulance.

14:28.619 --> 14:30.996
No. We talk in the casa.

14:59.775 --> 15:02.569
Sorry, but I'm not getting into
some creepy ambulance with a--

15:02.653 --> 15:04.780
Hey! What are you doing?

15:04.863 --> 15:05.864
Give me that.

15:09.618 --> 15:11.745
Are you crazy? They are listening.

15:11.828 --> 15:13.372
They will find out about our plan.

15:13.455 --> 15:18.293
I'm not an idiot. It's in airplane mode.
Airplane mode.

15:18.377 --> 15:20.546
No signal. Give it to me. Give it.

15:20.629 --> 15:23.799
No. Give it! Give… it!

15:24.383 --> 15:25.634
- No!
- No.

15:26.969 --> 15:28.762
Goddamn it.

15:32.683 --> 15:33.934
Are you kidding me?

15:37.229 --> 15:38.230
You know what?

15:38.730 --> 15:42.276
You can get back in your
ambulancia and fuck right off.

15:42.359 --> 15:43.527
I'm finito.

15:51.034 --> 15:53.453
- Carol Sturka.
- Unknown word or name.

15:54.037 --> 15:55.038
Bye.

16:12.181 --> 16:14.725
Well this is going just great.

16:23.567 --> 16:25.235
This sucks.

16:44.713 --> 16:46.632
Nine thousand kilometers for this shit.

16:47.633 --> 16:48.842
Shut your trap.

17:29.925 --> 17:33.679
Okay. You win.
Telephone, yes. Ambulance, no.

17:33.762 --> 17:35.013
But I need an umbrella.

18:01.248 --> 18:02.249
Come. Here.

18:04.751 --> 18:08.463
Y por qué? Big time por qué.

18:15.012 --> 18:16.972
These weirdos have eyes up above.

18:19.558 --> 18:21.518
They can read lips from space.

18:21.602 --> 18:24.605
So, let's go inside.
The drones can't spy on us there.

18:31.486 --> 18:34.448
Of course they can.
With microphones. Spy microphones.

18:34.531 --> 18:36.450
You think they planted a bug in my house?

18:40.913 --> 18:43.207
- An insect? With an insect?
- Ins… no, not a… not a ins…

18:43.290 --> 18:44.875
not an insect. A bug.

18:45.542 --> 18:47.294
Wait. Stop. Not you.

18:52.299 --> 18:54.760
Why would they spy on us inside my house?

19:00.974 --> 19:03.685
You are against them, no?
I watched your video.

19:07.648 --> 19:10.192
Why would the weirdos send me that video?

19:10.275 --> 19:11.276
I asked them to.

19:13.946 --> 19:14.947
Carol Sturka.

19:18.825 --> 19:20.327
Unknown word or name.

19:20.410 --> 19:22.621
Why would they help two humans
come together to destroy them?

19:22.704 --> 19:24.623
Destroy, I… Wait, I never said "destroy".

19:29.962 --> 19:30.963
These weirdos are evil.

19:33.131 --> 19:34.716
They have stolen everyone's soul.

19:38.220 --> 19:40.472
If we can't fix them,
they are better off dead.

19:41.598 --> 19:44.101
- They're still human beings.
- They are not human.

19:44.184 --> 19:46.728
Yes, they are. They are… They are.

19:46.812 --> 19:49.606
They're human. They're just…
They're just… They're different.

19:49.690 --> 19:52.067
I mean, they're weird, yes.

19:53.151 --> 19:55.445
- Too nice, yes, but they're not--
- Slow, slow.

19:58.156 --> 20:00.075
They are not evil.

20:02.286 --> 20:03.996
They wouldn't even kill an ant.

20:10.043 --> 20:12.880
And isn't it evil to value a man
the same as an ant?

20:14.173 --> 20:17.384
Have you even tried talking to them?
You could learn a thing or two.

20:17.926 --> 20:19.553
They can't lie. Did you know that?

20:29.897 --> 20:31.648
You said the weirdos abandoned you?

20:33.358 --> 20:35.569
Yep. For 40 days.

20:40.991 --> 20:41.992
Why they come back?

20:48.123 --> 20:49.124
I don't know.

20:49.666 --> 20:50.918
Why can't they pick an apple?

20:54.713 --> 20:56.882
- This is estúpido.
- Esto es stupid.

20:56.965 --> 20:57.966
I'm going inside.

21:30.666 --> 21:33.252
Told ya. No micro-fono.

21:34.294 --> 21:35.295
Happy?

21:52.187 --> 21:53.397
I don't speak snap.

22:07.828 --> 22:08.829
Please?

22:23.719 --> 22:27.097
What about the 11 other survivors?
Did they respond to your video?

22:27.181 --> 22:28.432
- Nope.
- No.

22:33.770 --> 22:35.272
They didn't even want to talk?

22:35.355 --> 22:36.940
Not to me.

22:38.358 --> 22:40.819
But I bet they'd love
your sparkling personality.

22:47.534 --> 22:48.994
You're not gonna find anything.

22:51.496 --> 22:52.497
I need a drink.

22:53.332 --> 22:55.501
You need a drink? You need a drink.

23:03.050 --> 23:04.468
Hey. Do you mind?

23:06.136 --> 23:07.429
What the hell?

23:10.891 --> 23:14.228
Okay. Buddy, I don't know
how guests behave in Paraguay,

23:14.311 --> 23:15.646
but here in Albuquerque,

23:15.729 --> 23:20.025
you cockblock someone
from their booze, it's un grande mistako.

23:21.109 --> 23:22.277
You're not even listening.

23:27.366 --> 23:28.825
Unknown word or name.

23:28.909 --> 23:30.035
What the hell is that?

23:35.082 --> 23:36.083
A sensor maybe.

23:41.338 --> 23:43.966
- Hi, Carol.
- Have you been spying on me?

23:44.049 --> 23:47.010
- Spying?
- There is a thing in my liquor cabinet.

23:47.553 --> 23:48.554
What kind of thing?

23:48.637 --> 23:53.183
I don't know. A plastic, rectangular…
kinda tacky-looking…

23:53.267 --> 23:55.769
like something out of a James Bond movie.

23:56.353 --> 23:58.772
It sure as shit
didn't come with the cabinet.

23:58.856 --> 24:00.649
Did you put it there?

24:01.275 --> 24:03.610
Right. It wasn't us, Carol.

24:04.236 --> 24:07.823
Do you remember May of 2011?
You were freezing your eggs.

24:07.906 --> 24:09.157
Yeah. So?

24:09.241 --> 24:11.410
The device is a movement sensor.

24:11.493 --> 24:15.414
It detects when the cabinet is opened,
then records it.

24:16.456 --> 24:18.792
Again, we didn't put it there.

24:21.962 --> 24:22.963
Helen.

24:23.881 --> 24:24.923
Sorry, Carol.

24:31.388 --> 24:32.389
No, no, no.

24:33.807 --> 24:34.808
It's all right.

24:37.227 --> 24:38.270
I'll call you later.

24:49.823 --> 24:50.824
It wasn't them.

24:53.368 --> 24:55.454
No "weirdos."

24:55.954 --> 24:57.080
Who?

24:59.374 --> 25:00.501
Mi esposa.

25:01.752 --> 25:02.961
She didn't like my…

25:06.256 --> 25:07.549
Now I really need a drink.

25:10.219 --> 25:11.762
Who you talk to on the teléfono?

25:12.804 --> 25:15.766
Them. Always them.

25:17.059 --> 25:19.144
The "Others."

25:25.526 --> 25:26.527
I'm tired.

25:27.277 --> 25:28.820
We save the world mañana.

25:51.927 --> 25:53.387
So…

25:55.889 --> 25:57.850
the kitchen has plenty of food.

26:01.061 --> 26:05.732
There are fresh sheets on the bed,
towels in the bathroom.

26:13.907 --> 26:16.493
We'll talk more tomorrow. Good night.

26:17.452 --> 26:18.912
Sleep tight.

26:21.832 --> 26:22.833
Who is this house?

26:24.710 --> 26:28.881
I think their name is Wilson.

26:32.634 --> 26:35.429
Look, I'll square it up with them
if they ever come back.

26:36.013 --> 26:37.848
Jesus, that would be
a great problem to have.

26:41.018 --> 26:42.186
This is not your house.

26:43.187 --> 26:46.481
It's no me house, no? I no stay.

26:47.316 --> 26:51.195
So that big yellow thing
parked outside is your ambulancia?

26:51.278 --> 26:52.988
Go sleep in that for all I care.

26:54.114 --> 26:55.866
My vodka is getting warm.

26:55.949 --> 26:57.284
And you're welcome.

27:26.480 --> 27:29.483
Hello, Manousos.
We are so happy to hear from you.

27:29.566 --> 27:31.401
What can we do for you?

27:31.485 --> 27:33.987
Am I speaking with the same
weirdo who Carol Sturka was talking to?

27:34.071 --> 27:36.490
No. That was another individual.

27:38.033 --> 27:41.119
What is the name of this individual?

27:42.037 --> 27:43.080
Zosia.

27:45.040 --> 27:46.959
I want to speak with Zosia.

28:55.027 --> 28:56.278
The fuck?

29:22.679 --> 29:23.680
Hi, Carol.

29:26.058 --> 29:27.434
What the hell is going on here?

29:28.268 --> 29:29.520
What are you doing?

29:30.854 --> 29:33.607
- You say I need talk. I talk.
- Not to her.

29:34.608 --> 29:35.692
What did you talk about?

29:36.735 --> 29:39.821
Zosia? What did you tell him?

29:41.823 --> 29:44.785
Todo. ¿Cómo se dice?

29:45.327 --> 29:46.328
Everything.

29:47.663 --> 29:48.664
Everything.

29:50.082 --> 29:51.708
I know what todo means.

29:53.001 --> 29:54.002
Come on, we're going.

29:58.549 --> 30:00.050
Zosia. Now.

30:24.867 --> 30:26.702
Send me another one.

30:43.886 --> 30:44.887
Todo.

30:45.554 --> 30:46.889
Todo, todo?

30:47.639 --> 30:50.559
What kind of everything did you tell him?

30:50.642 --> 30:52.102
- Sorry, Carol.
- Did you tell him…

30:54.563 --> 30:56.064
What exactly did you tell him?

30:57.065 --> 30:59.026
We didn't volunteer anything.

30:59.526 --> 31:02.738
He asked us specific questions,
detailed questions.

31:02.821 --> 31:05.199
He was very thorough and insistent.

31:05.282 --> 31:06.283
And…

31:07.034 --> 31:09.912
It's our nature. We had to answer him.

31:10.412 --> 31:13.624
Yeah. You had to. Right. I know.

31:14.208 --> 31:16.251
Why do you have to be so fucking honest?

31:16.335 --> 31:19.630
- It's just not in us to lie to you.
- Yeah, but to me, not to him.

31:21.006 --> 31:27.346
I know this is hard to understand,
but we love him the same as we love you.

31:31.266 --> 31:32.267
No.

31:34.478 --> 31:37.940
You can't love him the same.
It's not the same. It's different.

31:39.566 --> 31:40.567
He is a stranger.

31:40.651 --> 31:43.237
You barely know him.
You told me so yourself.

31:43.320 --> 31:44.530
And we… we're…

31:47.032 --> 31:48.033
You're my…

31:49.993 --> 31:50.994
You are my…

31:54.331 --> 31:55.541
You're my chaperone.

31:57.251 --> 31:58.252
Mine.

32:00.087 --> 32:01.088
Yes.

32:02.631 --> 32:03.632
That's true.

32:04.341 --> 32:06.176
- But--
- I want you to stay away from him.

32:06.260 --> 32:07.511
All right?

32:07.594 --> 32:09.805
I mean, did you see that machete?

32:10.764 --> 32:14.935
And you should hear the things
he says about you. Weirdos. Evil so--

32:15.018 --> 32:16.854
- What are you doing?
- Sorry, Carol.

32:16.937 --> 32:18.397
Something's about to happen.

32:18.480 --> 32:19.523
What?

32:19.606 --> 32:21.567
Please. Don't be alarmed.

32:23.443 --> 32:24.444
Zosia?

32:28.365 --> 32:29.700
Zosia?

32:29.783 --> 32:31.952
Jesus. Zosia! Zos…

32:35.289 --> 32:36.832
Hey. Hey!

32:37.958 --> 32:40.919
What's happening? I didn't even…
I wasn't… How…

32:46.008 --> 32:47.259
Shit.

32:58.395 --> 32:59.396
Jesus.

32:59.980 --> 33:02.191
Get the hell away from him.

33:03.192 --> 33:04.526
Hey.

33:04.610 --> 33:05.611
Hey.

33:07.029 --> 33:08.030
Hey!

33:11.909 --> 33:12.910
Hey.

33:52.699 --> 33:54.451
You're a psycho, you know that?

33:54.535 --> 33:57.329
Do you have any idea how many people
you've probably just killed?

34:01.625 --> 34:02.626
Hey.

34:03.335 --> 34:04.962
You're okay. You're okay.

34:05.045 --> 34:06.755
Just take it easy.

34:13.469 --> 34:15.973
What the fuck?

34:46.378 --> 34:47.379
Rick.

34:48.797 --> 34:50.382
I know you are there.

34:52.259 --> 34:53.260
I help you.

34:55.929 --> 34:56.929
I am here.

34:59.099 --> 35:02.436
Listen, Rick. I am here.

35:06.356 --> 35:08.692
You come back. Yes?

35:10.068 --> 35:11.069
You can do it.

35:14.948 --> 35:16.909
Listen, listen. Listen, Rick.

35:17.492 --> 35:19.995
You remember. Remember?

35:25.626 --> 35:28.879
You are there. You are there.
But you come back.

35:29.713 --> 35:32.925
Rick. I know you are there.
But you can remember. You…

35:33.008 --> 35:35.761
You can come back. You can come back.

35:36.595 --> 35:37.971
I am here.

35:38.055 --> 35:41.266
Listen to me, Rick. Rick, look at me.

35:53.237 --> 35:55.239
Back away. Now.

36:08.126 --> 36:09.127
Hey.

36:17.511 --> 36:19.346
Here. Lean up against the chair.

36:32.943 --> 36:33.986
You all right?

36:35.529 --> 36:36.530
Yeah.

36:39.199 --> 36:40.617
Could we have some water?

36:41.159 --> 36:42.286
Yeah. Yeah, of course.

36:53.255 --> 36:54.256
Thank you.

37:03.182 --> 37:06.101
Slow. Go… Go slow.

37:16.904 --> 37:17.988
You sure you're okay?

37:19.573 --> 37:21.658
Yeah. Thirsty, is all.

37:22.326 --> 37:23.327
We'll…

37:25.996 --> 37:28.081
I'll be fine. Thanks.

37:35.088 --> 37:36.632
Would you like to know who that is?

37:37.257 --> 37:38.258
I know who that is.

37:59.363 --> 38:00.531
It wasn't me this time.

38:05.369 --> 38:06.495
Screw you too, Laxmi.

38:16.630 --> 38:17.840
Carol, I'm so sorry.

38:18.924 --> 38:20.259
You know what we have to do.

38:55.252 --> 38:56.670
Where's Manousos, Carol?

38:57.296 --> 38:58.922
He is fine. Don't worry about him.

39:00.757 --> 39:04.219
For what it's worth, you should know
he did warn us first.

39:04.887 --> 39:05.888
Before he…

39:07.806 --> 39:08.807
did what he did.

39:22.321 --> 39:24.198
Please tell him
we're sorry it came to this.

40:10.410 --> 40:13.580
They're leaving again.
All of them, the whole city.

40:15.666 --> 40:16.750
I tried to tell you.

40:23.465 --> 40:24.466
So what?

40:29.680 --> 40:32.391
It was worth it. Completely.
Now I know much more.

40:37.479 --> 40:40.858
You were right. I think there's a way
to put things back in their place.

40:43.402 --> 40:44.403
Come on.

40:45.988 --> 40:47.155
Now the work begins.

40:54.204 --> 40:55.372
Carol Sturka.

40:55.455 --> 40:56.540
Unknown word or name.

40:59.418 --> 41:00.919
There's water and power.

41:02.087 --> 41:05.549
If you need anything else,
food or whatever, dial zero.

41:12.931 --> 41:13.932
Carol Sturka…

41:15.601 --> 41:18.812
Unknown word or name. Do you want to
save the world or get the girl?

45:02.327 --> 45:03.620
Thank you.

45:04.621 --> 45:05.622
Here you go.

45:05.706 --> 45:07.082
Okay.

45:15.340 --> 45:16.341
That's good.

45:23.348 --> 45:24.641
You seem pretty quiet.

45:24.725 --> 45:25.851
No. I was just thinking.

45:26.351 --> 45:27.686
Whatcha thinking?

45:27.769 --> 45:28.770
Nothing.

45:32.191 --> 45:33.192
No, I was…

45:35.652 --> 45:40.240
I was just wondering if you,
the first you,

45:40.324 --> 45:42.326
- the unjoined Zosia you…
- I understand.

45:42.409 --> 45:43.744
…if she…

45:46.413 --> 45:49.875
Did she have someone? In her past?

45:51.210 --> 45:53.921
She did. It was a long time ago.

45:55.589 --> 45:58.217
And what happened to them?

46:00.427 --> 46:03.889
Are they in there?
Like, with you right now?

46:05.140 --> 46:06.141
No.

46:07.518 --> 46:08.519
They're not.

46:15.025 --> 46:16.026
Man, I'm sorry.

46:19.404 --> 46:22.324
I don't think I'm good at
just feeling good.

46:25.410 --> 46:26.411
What does that to you?

46:27.120 --> 46:30.916
- Does what?
- Like, makes you happy.

46:32.084 --> 46:33.627
Like in our bodies. What chemicals?

46:34.753 --> 46:36.421
There's a mix.

46:36.505 --> 46:43.011
Serotonin, dopamine,
vasopressin, oxytocin of course.

46:44.096 --> 46:45.097
Fun fact.

46:45.889 --> 46:50.602
A study of zebra fish seems to imply
that oxytocin is responsible

46:50.686 --> 46:53.856
for the development of empathy
in vertebrate species

46:54.356 --> 46:55.983
about 200 million years ago.

46:58.277 --> 47:02.197
I must have every happy chemical
flowing in my bloodstream.

47:05.117 --> 47:07.411
I keep thinking it's gonna go away,
but then it doesn't.

47:10.706 --> 47:11.790
And I don't want it to.

47:12.541 --> 47:13.542
I'm glad.

47:15.252 --> 47:16.670
And it only gets better.

47:22.551 --> 47:23.635
Better?

47:28.015 --> 47:31.143
You're not talking about
the joining, are you?

47:33.562 --> 47:35.230
That's not even…

47:36.315 --> 47:38.192
You told me that you needed my stem cells.

47:39.193 --> 47:40.319
What, did that change?

47:40.819 --> 47:42.529
No. That's right.

47:43.030 --> 47:45.115
So without my stem cells,
you can't convert me.

47:46.408 --> 47:51.330
And if I don't expressly give you my
consent to jam a giant needle in my ass,

47:51.413 --> 47:55.334
then you can't take them,
and I stay me. Right?

47:58.504 --> 47:59.963
That would be correct.

48:01.715 --> 48:02.716
Would be.

48:06.720 --> 48:10.682
There's no other way
to get my stem cells, is there?

48:19.316 --> 48:20.901
If there wasn't, you'd say so.

48:26.949 --> 48:27.950
So there is a way.

48:48.762 --> 48:49.763
My eggs.

48:50.973 --> 48:52.349
The ones I froze with Helen.

48:55.644 --> 48:56.812
You have them, don't you?

49:03.318 --> 49:04.319
We do.

49:05.404 --> 49:07.656
And you can make those
into stem cells, can't you?

49:07.739 --> 49:10.409
It takes time and patience,
plus a bit of luck.

49:10.492 --> 49:11.660
But you're working on it.

49:14.580 --> 49:15.581
We are.

49:16.164 --> 49:18.959
You have to understand
how beautiful it is, Carol.

49:19.585 --> 49:21.920
You'll see why we have to share it.

49:22.421 --> 49:25.757
As happy as you've been,
that's only the tip of the iceberg.

49:26.758 --> 49:30.637
In fact, Kusimayu.
You remember the young Peruvian girl?

49:31.346 --> 49:32.472
She just joined us.

49:33.056 --> 49:38.187
And I promise you,
she's happier than she's ever been.

49:39.855 --> 49:42.024
You can hear that
straight from her if you like.

49:42.107 --> 49:43.317
How long do I have?

49:44.860 --> 49:47.779
Induced pluripotent stem cells
can be very fragile,

49:47.863 --> 49:49.489
- and we're dealing with haploid--
- How long?

49:53.410 --> 49:54.536
A month.

49:54.620 --> 49:57.122
Hopefully no more than two or three.

50:07.591 --> 50:09.426
If you loved me, you wouldn't do this.

50:11.178 --> 50:12.179
Carol.

50:14.306 --> 50:19.603
Please understand we have to do this
because we love you.

50:23.065 --> 50:25.150
Because I love you.

50:32.991 --> 50:33.992
Carol.

54:48.413 --> 54:49.540
You win.

54:53.877 --> 54:54.878
We save the world.

54:59.466 --> 55:00.467
Carol Sturka.

55:03.929 --> 55:04.930
What is this?

55:06.306 --> 55:07.307
Atom bomb.
